From c8b4ee51fd05fbbce929496b1d5496297fddc912 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Meenan <pmeenan@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] enc: compute bit costs, clustering and block splitting in
 f64 like C

C does BitsEntropy, PopulationCost, histogram bit_cost_, HistogramPair /
ClusterCostDiff, FindBlocks (insert_cost, cost, block_switch_cost),
BitCost, the greedy splitter entropies and ChooseContextMap /
ShouldCompress in double, with FastLog2 (double log2 for v >= 256). Rust
used f32 and the 16-bit FastLog2u16 table (which also truncated counts
>= 65536). This flipped block splits and cluster assignments at q10/q11.

FindBlocks now runs C's scalar double DP; insert_cost is kept as f64 bit
patterns in a u64 allocation because BrotliAlloc has no f64 allocator.
The 8xf32 SIMD update_cost_and_signal is removed.

Also run 10 block-split refinement iterations at q11 like C
(quality < HQ_ZOPFLIFICATION_QUALITY ? 3 : 10); Rust used 3.
